e8621b55de3a3a9c646edd59fb1c26372db042e230f9d2d3ec5a4e08d329361","taskId":"container-recipe"},{"mergeCommit":"e4ac78a9ba2a84aca3baec47a4698602a2f3b850","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/instruments-16ab40e19244fd0f","revision":"sha256:16ab40e19244fd0f9cde08858a2c348ff99e701e0a8ce46b6e99fc84b6d36c5b","taskId":"instruments"},{"mergeCommit":"b474021c40d16a6bd0fce9ac2b9002b4e6538cc4","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/host-tooling-ab66c582012f053f","revision":"sha256:ab66c582012f053ffa092301faf6a9b042d52ad26c6baa1b6d149083241af99d","taskId":"host-tooling"},{"mergeCommit":"71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/bench-harness-3a8882e61c9b2ce9","revision":"sha256:3a8882e61c9b2ce9ef7a7904e06778f0284df952e4a68deb4f8e6e1caba1a225","taskId":"bench-harness"}],"checkpoints":[],"remaining":["proxy-tooling","morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package","cp-weights","cp-build","cp-smoke","cp-proxy","cp-tp2","cp-bench","cp-close"],"frontier":["morning-ledger"],"diagnoses":[{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/3","diagnosis":"Failed the ownership gate conflict-domains because attempt 1 never committed anything: HEAD is still the base revision 71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa and all four produced artifacts sit untracked in the worktree, so the driver aborted with \"spec-build-driver: agent left uncommitted changes; commit the task before ownership validation\" and the finalMessage capture timed out with no worker outcome envelope. The work product itself looks substantially complete and in-boundary — scripts/make-proxy.sh, scripts/run-proxy.sh, and tests/test_proxy_tooling.py are all inside the conflict domains [redacted-token] the scripts are syntax-clean, and scripts/run-proxy.sh contains the literal results/receipts/proxy.json path the sole acceptance criterion greps for. The failure is purely that the attempt ended dirty rather than committed. One live boundary hazard explains why a naive \"git add -A\" would fail again: the untracked path results/receipts/proxy.json is a runtime receipt emitted by an actual serve run and is NOT inside any conflict domain, so committing it would make the same conflict-domains gate fail for the opposite reason. Attempt 2 steering: 1) Preserve the three existing in-domain files as they are; re-derive nothing and do not rewrite the scripts wholesale — this is a stateless reconcile over work already present in the lane. 2) Remove the out-of-domain artifact results/receipts/proxy.json from the worktree before committing (it is disposable runtime output that scripts/run-proxy.sh regenerates), so the tree is clean and no commit touches a path outside the domains. Do not add it to .gitignore or any other file, since those paths are also out of domain. 3) Stage exactly scripts/make-proxy.sh, scripts/run-proxy.sh, and tests/test_proxy_tooling.py — nothing else — and commit on the assigned branch tally-work/flashnext-cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling. Do not push or merge. 4) Before committing, self-check the acceptance criterion locally: bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'results/receipts/proxy.json' scripts/run-proxy.sh. 5) After the commit, verify with git status --porcelain that the tree is empty and with git show --stat that every path in the commit begins with scripts/make-proxy.sh, scripts/run-proxy.sh, or tests/. 6) Return the final result envelope as the last message so the adapter's finalMessage capture projects instead of timing out. Note for the record, not for fixing here: the receipt from the attempted run recorded status fail with an engine-core OOM during boot and an amdsmi absence in the container. Those are pair-lane and fork-lane concerns outside this task's authorized paths and outside its single acceptance criterion; attempt 2 must not chase them and must not widen scope to make a live serve pass.","taskId":"proxy-tooling","verdict":"retry"},{"attempt":2,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/4","diagnosis":"Failed the ownership gate conflict-domains with an empty lane rather than a boundary violation: the worker session produced no work at all on attempt 2. Verified in the assigned worktree at /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/667bc3eb0212/proxy-tooling: HEAD is still the prepared base, git log base..HEAD is empty, and git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all is completely silent — there are no untracked artifacts, no stash entries, and the only reflog records are the lane's own branch creation and prepare-time reset. scripts/ contains only the pre-existing build-engine.sh, mirror-substrate.sh, receipts-verify.py, run-smoke.sh, run-tp2.sh, stage-weights-both.sh, stage-weights.sh, verify-fork.sh; tests/ contains only the four pre-existing test modules. Neither scripts/make-proxy.sh nor scripts/run-proxy.sh nor any new file under tests/ was ever created this attempt, so the gate's stderr \"agent produced no commit relative to the prepared base\" is literal and no path was named as offending. This is a different failure mode from attempt 1, which did produce three in-domain files and merely left them uncommitted; the driver error here is the adapter fault result-projection-timeout with exitEvidencePassed false, meaning the spec-build-driver never captured a finalMessage and no worker outcome envelope exists — the session yielded neither a commit, nor a dirty tree, nor an outcome claim. Two further machinery facts support a session fault over a worker mistake. First, attempt 1 ran in lane cac9adc5400c and attempt 2 ran in a freshly prepared lane 667bc3eb0212; the earlier lane directory no longer exists, so the attempt-1 steering to reconcile statelessly over work already present in the lane addressed artifacts that were destroyed with the old lane and could not have been preserved. Second, the prepare-time reset in this lane is the only mutation recorded, so nothing the worker did was overwritten. There is no evidence of an out-of-task cause: the task's authority is intact, its sole acceptance criterion touches only scripts/make-proxy.sh, scripts/run-proxy.sh and the receipt string, its conflictDomains scripts/make-proxy.sh, scripts/run-proxy.sh and tests are sufficient for the goal, and dependencies are empty. There is likewise no actionable in-task fix to steer, because no code was written to critique. The correct disposition is a machinery retry against the bounded machinery-retry budget so the driver actually runs a worker session to completion and projects its final message; a content retry is unavailable regardless, since this attempt exhausts the hard two-attempt cap. If a re-run under the machinery budget again ends with zero filesystem effect and exitEvidencePassed false, the driver or adapter itself is at fault and the campaign should notify the operator rather than consume further budget.","taskId":"proxy-tooling","verdict":"blocked"}],"retries":[],"outcomes":[],"deferrals":[{"taskId":"cp-weights","waitingOn":["morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-build","waitingOn":["morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-smoke","waitingOn":["morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-proxy","waitingOn":["morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-tp2","waitingOn":["morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-bench","waitingOn":["morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-close","waitingOn":["rdma-package"]}],"blocked":[{"blockedBy":["proxy-tooling"],"taskId":"proxy-tooling"},{"blockedBy":["proxy-tooling"],"taskId":"cp-proxy"},{"blockedBy":["proxy-tooling"],"taskId":"cp-tp2"},{"blockedBy":["proxy-tooling"],"taskId":"cp-bench"},{"blockedBy":